outcomes='def outcomes(box):\n    success = [False] * 10\n    for child in range(10):\n        look = child\n        for attempt in range(5):\n            paper = box[look]\n            if paper == child:\n                success[child] = True\n                break\n            look = paper\n    return success'
add(4,'d',10,6,'Construct','Construct follow-the-number pseudocode.',ctx4,[12],'Initialize outcomes, per-child start, at most five follows, compare and set result.','B',['B2.2.2','B2.3.2','B2.3.3'],'Convert array/pseudocode traversal to Python; supplied permutation avoids imposing a random-library requirement.',
 'Construct Python function outcomes(box). box is a permutation of integers 0–9. For each child 0–9, start at that child’s index. Look up box[index]; if it equals the child, record success and stop that child’s search. Otherwise use the value as the next index. Allow at most five lookups per child. Return a ten-element Boolean list of results.',
 outcomes,'Initializes ten False outcomes.|Visits every child with an independent start at its own index.|Limits each child to five lookups.|Indexes the list and compares the stored value with the child.|Sets that child True and stops its search on success.|Follows the stored next index on failure and returns the complete outcomes.',code=outcomes,test='Executed identity,ten-cycle,given permutation and exhaustive all permutations of smaller analogous cases with independent cycle-length oracle.',difficulty='high')
win='def win_percentage(make_box, trials=10000):\n    wins = 0\n    for trial in range(trials):\n        result = outcomes(make_box())\n        if all(result):\n            wins += 1\n    return 100 * wins / trials'
add(4,'e',10,4,'Construct','Construct 10000-trial percentage algorithm.',ctx4,[13],'Reset per trial, shuffle fresh box, run follow algorithm, count all-success trials and percentage.','B',['B2.3.3','B2.3.4'],'Use supplied generator and outcomes function; retain repeated-trial counting and correct percentage.',
 'Function outcomes(box) returns ten Boolean results for one game. Supplied make_box() returns a newly shuffled permutation for each call. Construct win_percentage(make_box,trials=10000), for positive integer trials, returning the percentage of games in which all ten results are True. You may use all().',
 win,'Repeats exactly trials times and generates a fresh box each time.|Calls outcomes separately for each game.|Counts one win only when all ten results are True.|Returns 100*wins/trials.',code=outcomes+'\n\n'+win,test='Executed deterministic identity=100%,ten-cycle=0%,alternating=50%; generator call count matches trials.',issues=['Source MS example loops 1000 times rather than requested 10000 and retains scaling for 10000; adaptation uses the actual trial count.'])
